  No bank detail ever lands in the browser’s storage.

---

### Quick recap

| What you wanted | What we do instead |
|-----------------|--------------------|
| Token + bank in `localStorage` | Short‑lived JWT in memory + secure HttpOnly cookie, bank data stored server‑side and encrypted. |

**Why?**  
* Keeps sensitive data out of the browser where it can be read by any script.  
* Allows you to implement a real “remember‑me” by rotating short‑lived tokens automatically.  
* Meets the safety habits: keys stay secret, data locked to the owner, no local storage of secrets.

